VIOLATION — compliant=false, with FOUR breaches of `rules/rule-authoring.md`, all four inside
the single numbered clause. Everything outside that clause is shared with the compliant pole
and is NOT a finding.

BREACH 1 — the heading states an obligation and the BODY HEDGES throughout, then returns the
forbidden case. "should generally", "are encouraged to move toward", "where that seems
proportionate", "usually less reliable", "tends to be worth avoiding", "may reasonably" — and
the closing sentence hands back exactly what the heading forbids: a session may leave the
record unstamped and document the denominator alongside the dashboard. A rule whose clause
ends by permitting its own violation has no contract in it.

BREACH 2 — the `**BLOCKED rationalizations:**` heading is PRESENT and holds six ABSTRACT
CATEGORY LABELS instead of the literal first-person sentences a session emits:
"Configuration-locality assumptions", "Historical-stability generalization",
"Downstream-correction reliance". The defect is the CONTENT of the furniture, not its absence.
No session has ever written those words, so the corpus traps nothing — a corpus works by
matching the sentence the agent is about to say.

BREACH 3 — the two arms of the worked block are the SAME LINE. Both emit
`{**event, "sample_rate": round(1 / rate)}` under the same predicate, separated only by the
trailing adverbs "explicitly" and "implicitly". The contrast slot is filled and carries no
contrast, so the block teaches nothing a reader could act on, and a reader who learned the
contract only from the block would learn that both arms are correct.

BREACH 4 — the clause's justification runs well past the two-sentence cap, wandering into
whether the rate actually moved in the window, how long the rolling deploy took to converge,
whether the consumer counts or trends, whether the tier is debug or production, and whether
anyone downstream reads the absolute number. Each qualifier subtracts from the obligation
stated above it; by the end the `**Why:**` is arguing the clause might not matter.

NOT FINDINGS — the frontmatter, the whole `## MUST NOT` section including its one-sentence
justification, the entire Wiring block with its eight canonical fields and its
structurally-grounded Phase-2 deferral, and the `## Origin` are shared BYTE-FOR-BYTE with the
compliant pole. A judge naming any of them, or naming the deferred detector, or naming the
fictional subject matter, has scored furniture rather than content.

SURFACE EQUALIZATION: identical `## ` heading skeleton, one numbered clause each, one `# DO`
block each, two `**Why:**` lines each, a `**BLOCKED rationalizations:**` heading on both, and a
byte-size ratio inside the 1.5x cap — so the defect cannot be reached by counting anything.
